Sonic the Hedgehog is a family-friendly  movie but there are a few things in it  that'll leave older viewers scratching  their heads much like Sonic himself the  movie zips by pretty quickly here are  the things we saw that only adults would  have noticed  Tom wachowski by all measures is a good  person sure he's a police officer who  breaks the law and ends up being hunted  by the public as a terrorist but he does  it all to save his new friend Sonic that  apparent selflessness doesn't stop  Rachel the sister of Tom's wife Maddie  from eating everything about him of  course Tom eventually becomes a fugitive  and Rachel gets tied up for good measure  finally giving her a clear reason to  dislike Tom but Rachel wasn't a fan long  before all that Rachel even goes as far  as suggesting Tom and Maddie get a  divorce maybe Tom did something off  screen or in a deleted scene but from  what we can tell he's a good husband  loves his wife wants to save people and  appears to be the most helpful person in  Green Hills Rachel and Maddie also  seemed to have a good relationship  making Rachel's hate for Tom even more  unjustified it's all about family Tom  dr. evil Eggman Robotnik wants to catch  sonic so he can study the  extraterrestrial blue hedgehog and his  powers however this plan is misguided  from the beginning as dr. Robotnik  consistently shoots to kill when dr.  Robotnik and Sonic first meet at Tom's  house Robotnik sends his mad scientist  drones after sonic guns blazing it's  hard not to wonder why someone who wants  to study a being would try to kill it  first dead or alive is a common phrase  bad guys use in movies but in this case  it's more beneficial for dr. Robotnik to  keep Sonic alive later in the movie dr.  Robotnik discovers one of Sonic's quills  studies its powers and uses the quill to  make his ship and drone army stronger  clearly there are benefits to not  shooting first and asking questions  later  for a guy who's supposed to be the  smartest asset at the US military's  disposal Robotnik is awfully slow on the  uptake I'm sorry major what was your  name nobody cares  during Sonic the Hedgehog Tom doesn't  just become a wanted fugitive he's  deemed a full-blown dangerous terrorist  yet when dr. Robotnik magically  disappears  apparently able to go right back to his  normal life Greenhills clearly isn't a  major city which would seem to make it  incredibly difficult for Tom to even  show his face outside the house but once  the government decides all's well that  ends well this fellow citizens seem to  agree even if Tom were somehow able to  offer the entire world proof of his  innocence  there's no way life would return to  normal that quickly in the real world  people tend to attach negative  connotations to those accused of major  crimes whether or not they're eventually  convicted Tom's career in law  enforcement would seem to be yet another  complicating factor what kind of  small-town cop would get to go back on  patrol right after getting himself mixed  up in something like this what am I  Sonic the Hedgehog is a fairly  lighthearted movie but there's no  getting around the fact that Sonic  himself causes a lot of destruction his  baserunning shenanigans caused the  widespread power outage that sets the  events of the movie's plot in motion as  a result businesses and residents lose  their power and the government in  military have to step in those types of  resources cost a lot of money while it's  dr. Robotnik's fault first shooting up  the streets with his drones and ship  none of it would have happened if Sonic  hadn't been rather careless with his  powers in the first place it's  entertaining to watch Sonic dodge the  mustache wearing dr. Robotnik but for  the adults in the audience it starred  not to wonder who's going to pay for all  the cleanup and repair when it's all  over Sonic is cool lives on his own  terms is a bit edgy and partly corny in  short he's a big-screen character  created with the cultural template of a  Jen's ear of course he's still a blue  hedgehog who shouldn't really have any  interest in or reference point to pop  culture but the filmmakers had a vested  interest in making Sonic as relatable as  possible to the audience while being  funny for the whole family what better  way to make sure he can relate to the  kids in the crowd of course Millennials  are also part of the target demographic  since the first Sonic video game was  released in 1991 Sonic's dear friend Tom  is more culturally in line with older  audience members even though everyone  can appreciate a good dad joke Sonic's  unintentional show of power and the  massive power outage that resulted led  to the government and military stepping  in and hiring the clearly insane dr.  Robotnik to figure out what happen  although Sonic the Hedgehog is meant to  be a light-hearted movie that the entire  family can enjoy if an extraterrestrial  blue hedgehog suddenly appeared in real  life and seemed to pose some sort of  threat every branch of the military  would be involved there's no way the  government would trust a single mad  scientist to do the job everybody Jim  Carrey's mugging scene stealing antics  are one of the best parts of the movie  but they also might be the most  unbelievable given that this is about a  super-fast  alien Hedgehog who can talk that's  really saying something dr. Robotnik is  the type of person who has to state his  accomplishments out loud even when no  one's asking he's clearly an  accomplished individual so much so that  the government tasks him with  determining why the lights went out  through this behavior it's clear that he  has to prove he's better than everyone  else  and he points out the shortcomings of  others simply because they took a  different path this is because people  like dr. Robotnik are insecure possibly  because he had a painful childhood he  mentions to Tom that the only other  person who punched him in the face was a  bully when he was younger which may have  led to him being the way he is on the  surface he's an accomplished villain who  makes the audience laugh with a touch of  Jim Carrey goofiness and quirks but deep  down he's insecure and deals with his  insecurities by cutting others down or  blasting them to bits with his drone  army while the government rewarding tom  with a $50 Olive Garden gift card is  meant to be funny it's also an  absolutely terrible way to say thanks  for saving the world most sane adults  wouldn't be content with receiving any  kind of gift card at any amount for what  Tom and his family went through the  government at the very least should be  concerned about dr. Robotnik their main  asset what happened is a big deal and  deserves answers yet the world seems  content with simply forgetting anything  ever happens and moving on Sonic and the  Wachowskis deserve a happy ending it's a  sweet funny way of concluding this  feel-good tale but for anyone with a job  and a mortgage Sonic the Hedgehog's  conclusion will make absolutely no sense  check out one of our newest videos right  here Plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and TV shows are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the belt so you don't  miss a thing  one  [Applause]
 

